# LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is `true` on this machine, so without this file the first
# checkout after the first commit rewrites every text file to CRLF on disk - and
# `cargo package` builds its tarball from the working tree, not from the index.
# The crate would then ship CRLF to readers on every platform, permanently: a
# publish cannot be withdrawn, only yanked from resolution.
#
# It matters here beyond tidiness because `tests/readme.rs` reads README.md
# through `include_str!` and splits table rows out of it. Those tests pass under
# CRLF - checked 2026-09-08 by converting the file and re-running - so this is
# about what the crate looks like to a reader rather than about a break.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files, so no line ending translation is attempted on them at all.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
